bly the one you'll  be most bummed you didn't know existed  this is the Internet and as such cats  are worshipped as gods caddy is a  documentary about the feral cats of  Istanbul the filmmakers took to the  streets to introduce viewers to the free  roaming felines that lead surprisingly  unique lives and the people who are  interact with them on a daily basis  Kaddi features kittens with necks for  slipping into hidden alleyway crevices  cats that keep a keen eye on the dogs  for the incoming fish market shipments  and furry faced friends perched upon  doorsteps and behind shop counters it  can be silly on the surface but caddy  has a big heart and though it's centered  around animals the film's narrative  feels utterly human very much a part of  the local culture and the community of  Istanbul the cats and kittens of kettie  remind us that were not born knowing  hatred or judgments illustrated through  the remarkable respect between man and  animal plus adorable kittens what's not  to love  thanks for watching click the loop icon  to subscribe to our YouTube channel plus  check out all this cool stuff we know  your love to  [Music]
 

